WEBVTT

00:34:00.010 --> 00:34:01.304
in candidates like Scott.

00:34:01.328 --> 00:34:04.264
RS: What we said was, "Your job is to try

00:34:04.288 --> 00:34:07.752
and get the person
sitting next to you a second interview.

00:34:07.776 --> 00:34:10.059
Make your partner look good."

00:34:10.083 --> 00:34:12.309
AG: Scott failed his audition.

00:34:12.333 --> 00:34:13.702
He was shy and very quiet,

00:34:13.726 --> 00:34:16.491
so his first impression
wasn't always glowing.

00:34:16.948 --> 00:34:19.211
A few months later, he tried again.

00:34:19.235 --> 00:34:21.378
SK: I remember just being more relaxed,

00:34:21.402 --> 00:34:22.656
made some jokes,

00:34:22.680 --> 00:34:25.678
tried to, you know,
bond with my pair partner.

00:34:25.702 --> 00:34:26.860
Because really,

00:34:26.884 --> 00:34:30.347
the working relationship is what helps
drive getting something done.